# Deploy

Run deployment commands from the repository root. The Makefile uses the
current npm release of `@google/clasp`, pinned by default to version 3.3.0, so
an outdated system `gclasp` package is not required.

Install the pinned deployment tools, then log in and inspect the projects:

```sh
make setup
make login
make build
make status
```

Clasp 3 no longer transpiles TypeScript during `push`. The Makefile uses the
pinned `ts2gas` package to build ignored `.clasp-build` staging directories and
points clasp at the generated JavaScript. `make status` therefore shows the
exact generated files that would be uploaded.

## Push scripts

Push deployable files changed relative to a Git ref:

```sh
make plan SINCE=origin/master
make push SINCE=origin/master
```

On a feature branch, `origin/master` is normally the correct comparison. If
the changes have already been merged and pulled into `master`, provide the
commit or tag of the last release instead:

```sh
make push SINCE=<last-release-ref>
```

Projects can also be selected explicitly:

```sh
make push PROJECTS="docs slides"
make push-theme
make push-all
```

Only Apps Script source and configuration files count as project changes.
README files, screenshots, tests, schemas, and npm metadata do not trigger a
push or release.

## Create a release

Preview the dependency-expanded release order, then release:

```sh
make plan SINCE=<last-release-ref>
make release SINCE=<last-release-ref> DESCRIPTION="Release description"
```

The release command:

1. pushes and versions changed `codemirror` and `theme` libraries;
2. writes their new versions into the Docs and Slides manifests;
3. pushes and versions directly changed or dependency-affected add-ons; and
4. prints every newly created Apps Script version.

If a library was released, review and commit the resulting changes to
`docs/appsscript.json` and `slides/appsscript.json`.

Releases require committed Apps Script files. `ALLOW_DIRTY=1` is available for
an intentional exception.

## Update existing deployments

Deployment updates are opt-in and require explicit IDs. This prevents the
release command from accidentally creating replacement deployments:

```sh
make release-deploy SINCE=<last-release-ref> \
  DOCS_DEPLOYMENT_ID=<docs-id> \
  SLIDES_DEPLOYMENT_ID=<slides-id>
```

After creating add-on versions, update the corresponding versions in the
[Google Workspace Marketplace SDK configuration](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/api/appsmarket-component.googleapis.com/googleapps_sdk?project=syntax-highlight-302620)
when required by the publication workflow.
